    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **283 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `namesakeCount` feature so that when an owner is created, the count of other owners sharing the same last name at that moment is captured and returned in the owner response.\n\nChanges made, following the existing pattern used for `membershipTier`/`customerCode`/`membershipNumber`:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** (entity) \u2014 added a `namesakeCount` `Integer` field mapped to the `namesake_count` column, with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `namesakeCount` integer property (`int32`, `minimum: 0`) to the `Owner` schema, which regenerates into `OwnerDto`. MapStruct auto-maps it by name.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 computes the count of existing owners sharing the new owner's last name (before saving, so it counts *other* owners) via a new `namesakeCount(String lastName)` helper. The comparison reuses the existing `normalize(...)` helper, so it ignores letter case and surrounding/repeated whitespace, consistent with the other duplicate-detection logic in this controller.\n\n4. **Schema files** (`h2`, `hsqldb`, `postgres`, `mysql`) \u2014 added the `namesake_count` column.\n\nThe count is evaluated at creation time and persisted on the owner, so it reflects the namesake count as of that moment and remains stable on later reads.",
